## 3 · When to read what

| Situation | First stop |
|---|---|
| Fresh session | skill `noc-contextualize` |
| Backend / frontend code | `CLAUDE/backend.md` / `CLAUDE/frontend.md` + `KB § PATTERNS/` |
| New/absorb product · ship/deploy · branch/dispatch · self-branch · wiring · container debug · cleanup | the matching `noc-*` skill |
| Specialist opinion mid-flight | agent `architect` / `security` / `compliance-reviewer` |
| Project lifecycle / `*-PROJECT.md` | `CLAUDE/projects.md` + `KB § PATTERNS/project-execution.md` |
| Migration · auth · OAuth · LGPD · anything else | `KB § INDEX.md` |

---

## 4 · Sync rule

CLAUDE.md, `CLAUDE/*`, `.claude/skills/`, `.claude/agents/`, `KB § INDEX.md` stay in sync — add/rename/delete a KB doc or skill/agent → every referencing layer updates the same commit. Pre-commit hook (`scripts/hooks/pre-commit`) runs `noctus.dev.kb_sync` and blocks on unresolved `KB §` pointers, unindexed KB docs, or a product missing its `02-LANDSCAPE.md` roster row. Manual: `python mcp/noctusai/cli.py --verify-kb-sync`. Bypass (rare): `--no-verify`.

> `KB § X` = `KNOWLEDGE-BASE/X`.
